m=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured go.etcd.io/raft/v3 library: serialized RawNode core and channel-owned Node wrapper, tracker/quorum/confchange, log/unstable and MemoryStorage interface support. Network delivery, actual durability and client state machine are caller responsibilities, not inspected external implementations.',protocol_contexts=['Per-group term, role, leader and log index/term','Simple or joint voting membership, learners and staged learners','Synchronous Ready/Advance or AsyncStorageWrites worker messages'],external_interfaces=['Node','RawNode','Storage','Ready','raftpb.Message'],ownership=['Node.run serializes events; RawNode is thread-unsafe and must be caller-serialized.','Caller owns transport and durable storage and applies configuration entries.'],source_ids=['s-raw-interface','s-node-loop','s-storage-interface','s-async-contract','s-node-completion-contract']),activities=acts,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='raft.switchToConfig pending read release',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-membership','b-reads','b-formation'],reason='Different commit producers have different read-release effects. Legal first-current-term commit history remains relevant; no completion guarantee assumed.',source_ids=['s-config-commit','s-ack-commit','s-release-reads']),dict(entry_point='Node.Advance before ApplyConfChange',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-application','b-authority','b-membership'],reason='Early completion acknowledgement may hide committed membership entries from the campaign scan. Applicability and legal history are unresolved.',source_ids=['s-node-completion-contract','s-election-entry','s-ready-completion']),dict(entry_point='Ready synchronous message persistence ordering',disposition='UNCLASSIFIED_PROTOCOL_RESPONSIBILITY',reason='README and doc.go overlap permission conflicts with stronger Ready ordering. Preserve conflicting contracts before any executable allegation.',source_ids=['s-readme-caller','s-doc-caller','s-ready-contract'],high_consequence=True)],core_overview=dict(status='usable',formation=path('Leader admits proposals, assigns term/index and emits append requests. Followers match predecessors, protect committed prefixes and defer append support until persistence. Leader tracks qualified replies and selects the active majority or both joint majorities, committing only an advancing current-term entry. It propagates commit through appends and bounded heartbeats; Ready/application consumes the prefix separately. Retry/probe/snapshot paths recover lagging replicas. Configuration application can recalculate commit with different quorum eligibility, but unlike append-reply advancement it does not release queued precommit reads.',['b-formation','b-recovery','b-persistence','b-membership','b-application'],['f-commit'],['s-ack-commit','s-log-commit','s-tracker','s-joint','s-replication-send','s-append-receive','s-ready-output','s-config-commit']),context=path('Campaigns require promotable membership and scan committed entries after applied for pending configurations. Real campaigns persist votes, aggregate eligible votes and elect an up-to-date leader; pre-vote preserves the term until support is obtained. Higher terms, same-term leader traffic to candidates and quorum loss remove authority; transfer requires caught-up target and times out. Reset clears per-election votes, remote match, read quorum contexts and transfer. Old-term messages cannot contribute ordinary support; committed log prefixes and old snapshot completion survive. Recovery rebuilds term/vote/configuration/log from caller storage.',['b-authority','b-membership','b-persistence','b-recovery'],['f-applied','f-commit'],['s-election-entry','s-candidate-follower','s-term-dispatch','s-leadership','s-reset-authority','s-transfer','s-initial-state','s-restore']),connection=path('Election log freshness and persistent term/vote constrain who may form future decisions; current-term commit and active voter quorums constrain advancement by that leader. Configurations take effect via ApplyConfChange, not at append. Their applied-history bookkeeping is consumed by campaign admission and proposal serialization. Thus application acknowledgement is authority-relevant. Delayed storage messages carry term/context to avoid using obsolete support, while committed decisions and application work are term-independent. Safe reads wait for current-term commitment and quorum context; pending precommit messages differ from the resettable readOnly map.',['b-authority','b-formation','b-membership','b-application','b-persistence','b-reads'],['f-applied','f-commit'],['s-election-entry','s-node-completion-contract','s-ready-completion','s-config-commit','s-storage-response','s-release-reads','s-read-acks']),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Applicability of early Advance before committed membership application and its effect on campaign eligibility.','Contract conflict on synchronous same-batch send/persist overlap.','Pending reads retained across reset and configuration-driven commit: narrower legal histories and permitted request loss need investigation.','Detailed storage failures, compaction concurrency, lease-clock bounds and special bootstrap histories remain outside this initial backbone.'],rationale='Representative formation and authority paths, their membership/persistence dependencies, old-work treatment, retries and consumption are sourced. Local completion-contract anomalies remain explicit rather than becoming unconditional Fact guarantees.'))
json.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2)
q=dict(question='When Node.Advance is used before application finishes, can raftLog.applied cause campaign admission to skip a committed configuration entry whose ApplyConfChange is still pending, and what caller obligation or alternative mechanism prevents stale-membership authority?',importance='If legally reachable, stale-membership campaigning could undermine eligibility and later quorum formation. This is potential consequence; neither a safety violation nor a legal execution history is established.',trigger_rationale='Node.Advance explicitly permits early acknowledgement; RawNode accepts that acknowledgement as MsgStorageApplyResp and hup scans only after applied. The separate ApplyConfChange callback supplies actual membership. Source contract investigation is cheaper and more decisive than an immediate safety test; the earlier queued-read discrepancy also depends on this premise, whereas synchronous persistence overlap has an independent unresolved contract conflict.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='source_review',source_ids=['s-node-completion-contract','s-raw-interface','s-ready-completion','s-apply-response','s-election-entry','s-campaign-test','s-node-loop'],participants=['Application driving Node/RawNode','Local follower or candidate','Voting peers'],objects=['Ready.CommittedEntries containing a configuration change','raftLog.applied','tracker.Config'],contexts=['AsyncStorageWrites=false','Serialized caller with durable Ready storage and application batches kept in order','Advance before pending ApplyConfChange'],event_paths=['Committed configuration delivered in Ready -> storage completed -> early Advance -> applied cursor advanced -> campaign before ApplyConfChange'],activity_classes=['A2','A5','A4'],behavior_ids=['b-application','b-authority'],fact_ids=['f-applied'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b-membership':'Actual voting configuration changes only through the separately applied callback, explaining why acknowledged progress may diverge from authority context.','b-persistence':'The legal prefix must finish persistence even if state-machine application is still pending.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['hup explicitly refuses committed configurations after applied.','RawNode.Advance wording says application has applied and saved progress; async apply responses explicitly require completed application.','Node.ApplyConfChange must be called when a committed configuration is observed, which may constrain the timing despite the general early-Advance permission.','Existing campaign test acknowledges application before allowing campaign; its helper behavior must be examined before interpreting it as a configuration-completion requirement.'],unknowns=['Does early-Advance permission cover membership-bearing batches or only ordinary commands/snapshots?','Does a source-backed legal API history reach campaigning before the actual membership callback despite all caller requirements?','If reachable, is the responsibility local campaign eligibility or only a broader consensus property requiring an additional producer history?'],priority=3)
x=dict(action='continue',rationale='Establish the usable both-core map and select the concrete application-progress/authority premise without asserting a defect.',map_path='map.json',sources=sources,question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['b-application','b-authority','b-reads','s-node-completion-contract','s-node-read-contract','s-election-entry'],answered='Completed source tracing for the representative formation/context backbone. The pending-read observation has a nontrivial protective premise: with completion-before-Advance, unapplied committed configurations block election, while committing previously uncommitted old configuration entries first requires a current-term leader commit that already releases reads. Node also explicitly allows silent ReadIndex loss, so an omitted release alone cannot establish bounded liveness. Early Advance is now the narrower authority premise to investigate; it can update the applied cursor independently of actual ApplyConfChange. This is a contract/history question, not a finding.',remaining=['Resolve early-Advance applicability and inspect the existing test helper before constructing a controlled schedule.','Preserve synchronous persistence-order contract conflict as an independent unmapped responsibility surface.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Map facts preserve acknowledged progress rather than assuming completed membership application. First Candidate focuses on its consumption in election admission.'))
